---
// Shared shell for paginated story-flow games — Daily Routines today,
// Woodcutter (in some form) eventually. Games where the pedagogy is
// "follow a linear narrative one chapter at a time, then take a quick
// quiz on what you read". Sister to:
//   - `CardMachineLayout` (reference-catalogue browser, deck of facts).
//   - `GridLayout` (foundational-set grid, scan a bounded chart).
//
// Carved out at the Routines port (2026-05-08) after `CardMachineLayout`
// failed the first-fit gate: viewport-locked overflow, two-pane layout,
// stacked deck DOM, and OLED-look right pane all collapse for a
// scrollable story page with a quiz at the end. See
// `src/data/routines.ts` header for the full decision rationale.
//
// Provides head meta, PWA wiring, navigation, settings modal, build
// info, and service worker auto-update handling. Each story game
// supplies its scene markup, controls, and inline quiz via the default
// slot plus a handful of props. Scrolling is allowed on `body.story`
// because story prose + an N-question quiz won't fit on a phone in
// 100 vh.

import '@/styles/global.css';
import '@/styles/story.css';

import BuildInfo from '@/components/BuildInfo.astro';
import GameNav from '@/components/GameNav.astro';
import SettingsModal from '@/components/SettingsModal.astro';

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  themeColor?: string;
  ogImage?: string;
  /** Used in service worker updates to construct the canonical page URL */
  pageUrl?: string;
  /** Inline lang attribute */
  lang?: string;
  /**
   * Visual palette for the story shell. Controls the CSS custom
   * properties defined in `story.css`. Leave undefined for the
   * default theme. Add new keys here as more story games land.
   *
   * `'addition'` (added 2026-05-15 for the Counting Friends game),
   * `'comparison'` (added 2026-05-18 for the More Friends game),
   * `'numberfriends'` (added 2026-05-18 — same day, later — for the
   * Number Friends game), `'patterns'` (added 2026-05-20 for the
   * Pattern Sequences game), and `'letterfriends'` (added 2026-05-25
   * for the Letter Friends game — first preschool-LITERACY game)
   * are not strictly story games, but reuse StoryLayout's wiring
   * (head, GameNav, SettingsModal, BuildInfo, SW registration, FOUC
   * handling) which is exactly what a single-scene-per-round stage
   * game needs.
   *
   * FIFTH-CONSUMER STAGELAYOUT DEFERRAL (2026-05-25, 5th time deferred).
   *
   * Per rule #5 ("refactor on second consumer"), the More Friends
   * ship was the natural trigger to carve a `StageLayout` sister
   * shell. We deferred. Number Friends was the third stage-game
   * ship; we deferred again. Pattern Sequences (2026-05-20) was
   * the fourth, at the original "fourth-game" trigger condition;
   * we deferred there too on revised criteria. Letter Friends
   * (2026-05-25) is the FIFTH stage-game ship — at the
   * already-revised "fifth-game" criterion. We're STILL deferring,
   * because the underlying logic that drove the previous deferrals
   * STILL hasn't changed:
   *
   *   1. The chrome differences between StoryLayout and a
   *      hypothetical StageLayout still amount to ONE thing: the
   *      `body.story` → `body.stage` class rename. Every game-
   *      specific style is already scoped under
   *      `body.story[data-theme='X']`, so the prefix is doing the
   *      isolation work that a body-class differentiator would do.
   *      Letter Friends ships using the exact same body-class shape
   *      as the cardinality triad and Pattern Sequences — no novel
   *      chrome requirement.
   *   2. The hypothetical StageLayout would re-import all the same
   *      head meta, GameNav, SettingsModal, BuildInfo, FOUC script,
   *      and SW registration — the entire `<head>` and `<body>`
   *      shell would be duplicated, not shared. So the carve
   *      doesn't actually deduplicate anything; it just relocates.
   *   3. Migrating addition.css + comparison.css + numberfriends.css
   *      + patterns.css + letterfriends.css from
   *      `body.story[...]` to `body.stage[...]` is mechanical churn
   *      (5 files × ~30 selectors each ≈ 150 replacements, one-time
   *      but irreversible without re-doing the same churn). And
   *      every stage-game test would need an updated body-class
   *      assertion.
   *
   * Re-revised trigger conditions for actually carving StageLayout
   * (after the 5-game data point):
   *   - A SIXTH stage-game ships AND a meaningful chrome
   *     difference emerges (different head meta, different header,
   *     a different settings panel, etc.). The "Nth game count"
   *     alone has now been deferred TWICE — the carve genuinely
   *     has to deduplicate something real. Through 5 games we've
   *     proven the body-class scope IS the deduplication mechanism.
   *   - OR the theme union grows to ≥7 keys and starts to feel
   *     genuinely unwieldy in code review.
   *   - OR a stage-only style primitive emerges that would belong
   *     in a stage-only stylesheet (none today: every game style
   *     is per-game).
   *
   * The shared *content* primitives across these games (theme
   * catalog, number-word helpers, common pedagogical patterns) ARE
   * refactored — see `src/lib/preschool-themes.ts`. That's where
   * the second-consumer carve actually happened. Letter Friends
   * uses the theme catalog (for ambient bg) but doesn't need the
   * number-word helpers — first preschool-math content primitive
   * NOT used by a literacy game, validating that the lib stays
   * scoped to math without a forced carve.
   */
  theme?:
    | 'routines'
    | 'woodcutter'
    | 'addition'
    | 'comparison'
    | 'numberfriends'
    | 'patterns'
    | 'letterfriends'
    | 'soundfriends'
    | 'numberbond'
    | 'sortingfriends'
    | 'weekfriends'
    | 'daysparade'
    | 'animalsounds'
    | 'feelingfriends'
    | 'oppositesfriends'
    | 'rhymetime'
    | 'wheresteddy'
    | 'memorymatch';
}

const {
  title,
  description,
  themeColor = '#ff9a56',
  ogImage = 'https://aakash-jain-1.github.io/kids-learning-games/assets/icon-512.svg',
  pageUrl,
  lang = 'en',
  theme,
} = Astro.props;

const canonicalUrl =
  pageUrl ??
  new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site ?? 'https://aakash-jain-1.github.io').href;
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang={lang}>
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content={themeColor} />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />

    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>📖</text></svg>"
    />

    <title>{title}</title>

    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />

    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />

    <!-- Apply saved dark-mode class before paint to avoid FOUC -->
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        try {
          var raw = localStorage.getItem('kids_settings_v1');
          if (!raw) return;
          var s = JSON.parse(raw);
          if (s && s.dark) document.documentElement.classList.add('pre-dark');
        } catch (e) {
          /* noop */
        }
      })();
    </script>
  </head>

  <body class="story" data-theme={theme}>
    <GameNav />

    <slot />

    <SettingsModal />
    <BuildInfo />

    <script>
      import { initSettings } from '@/lib/settings';
      initSettings();

      document.documentElement.classList.remove('pre-dark');
    </script>

    <script>
      import { registerSW } from 'virtual:pwa-register';
      registerSW({
        immediate: true,
        onRegisteredSW(_scriptUrl, registration) {
          if (registration) {
            setInterval(() => registration.update(), 60 * 60 * 1000);
          }
        },
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style is:global>
  html.pre-dark body.story {
    background: #2a1505;
    color: #ffe0c0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='routines'] {
    background: #2a1505;
    color: #ffe0c0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='woodcutter'] {
    background: #0a0f1f;
    color: #d4d8f0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='addition'] {
    background: #0a1020;
    color: #d4e0ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='comparison'] {
    background: #0a1020;
    color: #d4e0ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='numberfriends'] {
    background: #0a1020;
    color: #d4e0ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='patterns'] {
    background: #0a1020;
    color: #d4e0ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='numberbond'] {
    background: #0a1020;
    color: #d4e0ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='letterfriends'] {
    background: #1a0a14;
    color: #f0d4e0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='soundfriends'] {
    background: #1a0a14;
    color: #f0d4e0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='sortingfriends'] {
    background: #07211d;
    color: #d4f0ea;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='weekfriends'] {
    background: #0a0e26;
    color: #d4daff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='daysparade'] {
    background: #04201d;
    color: #d4f0ea;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='animalsounds'] {
    background: #05192a;
    color: #d4e8f8;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='feelingfriends'] {
    background: #14122b;
    color: #e4e4ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='oppositesfriends'] {
    background: #241a06;
    color: #fff4e0;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='rhymetime'] {
    background: #2a0a16;
    color: #ffe6ee;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='wheresteddy'] {
    background: #1b1030;
    color: #ece4ff;
  }
  html.pre-dark body.story[data-theme='memorymatch'] {
    background: #2a1206;
    color: #ffe8d6;
  }
</style>
